<article class="env-lemma" id="0BIW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BIW">Lemma <span data-tag="0BIW">15.52.9</span>.</a> Properties (A), (B), (C), (D), and (E) hold for $P(k \to R) =$“$R$ is geometrically reduced over $k$”. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Part (A) follows from the definition of geometrically reduced algebras (Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/030S" data-tag="030S">10.43.1</a>). Part (B) follows too: a ring is reduced if and only if all local rings are reduced. Part (C). This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/07QK" data-tag="07QK">15.43.1</a>. Part (D). This follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/033F" data-tag="033F">10.164.2</a>. Part (E). This follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C2Y" data-tag="0C2Y">10.43.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>